flavour|doctrine_tt_flux_arbitrage	0	Corporate engineers treat flux like capital: borrow hard and repay fast. Their venting schedules, copied from a captured Aurora's maintenance logs, let this ship dump heat faster and bleed it off steadily between volleys.
