flavour|nskr_volatile	0	A prototype flux injector from Kesteven R&D lets the crew trade staying power for tempo. The ship runs faster and fires quicker while its flux is low, then slows on both counts once flux climbs past half. The injector also enlarges the flux network, at the cost of shorter long-range fire and a tighter leash on strikecraft.
type|nskr_volatile|null|0	0	Weapon rate of fire changes with flux, from <good>40%</good> increased at no flux to <bad>40%</bad> reduced at full flux, with no change at half flux. Venting or being overloaded counts as full flux.
type|nskr_volatile|null|1	0	<good>67%</good> increased flux capacity.
type|nskr_volatile|null|2	0	<good>67%</good> increased flux capacity granted by each flux capacitor.
type|nskr_volatile|null|3	0	<good>+800</good> to range before falloff effectiveness applies.
type|nskr_volatile|null|4	0	<bad>50%</bad> less weapon range beyond the range threshold.
type|nskr_volatile|null|5	0	<bad>75%</bad> less strikecraft engagement range.
type|nskr_volatile|null|6	0	On hulls with Augmented Systems, <good>50%</good> reduced effect of the high-flux top speed and rate of fire penalties.
type-detail|nskr_volatile|null|0	0	Can't be allocated on phase ships.
type-detail|nskr_volatile|null|1	0	Mutually exclusive with <hullmod>hullmods</hullmod>:\n• <hullmod>Safety Overrides</hullmod>\n• <hullmod>Volatile Flux Injector</hullmod>\n\nMutually exclusive with <node>node</node>:\n• <node>Safety Overrides</node>
