flavour|tactical_superiority	0	Every spacer carries a TriPad, and a crew that learns to use Tri-Tachyon's own hardwired backdoors can talk combat objectives into handing over control. This ship captures combat objectives much faster.
type|tactical_superiority|null|0	0	<good>100%</good> more combat objective capture rate.
type|tactical_superiority|FRIGATE|0	0	<good>100%</good> more combat objective capture rate.
type|tactical_superiority|DESTROYER|0	0	<good>100%</good> more combat objective capture rate.
type|tactical_superiority|CRUISER|0	0	<good>100%</good> more combat objective capture rate.
type|tactical_superiority|CAPITAL_SHIP|0	0	<good>100%</good> more combat objective capture rate.
flavour|tania_carina_charge	0	Navarchy captains close on their targets at full burn, trusting old armor to take the blow while every gun fires into the point of contact. Crews who have fought beside Navarchy fleets drill this ship's gunners to fire the same way, so its shots land harder the faster it charges in.
type|tania_carina_charge|null|0	0	<good>0.08%</good> increased ballistic and non-beam energy weapon damage for every su/s of the ship's current speed.
type|tania_carina_charge|FRIGATE|0	0	<good>0.08%</good> increased ballistic and non-beam energy weapon damage for every su/s of the ship's current speed.
type|tania_carina_charge|DESTROYER|0	0	<good>0.08%</good> increased ballistic and non-beam energy weapon damage for every su/s of the ship's current speed.
type|tania_carina_charge|CRUISER|0	0	<good>0.08%</good> increased ballistic and non-beam energy weapon damage for every su/s of the ship's current speed.
type|tania_carina_charge|CAPITAL_SHIP|0	0	<good>0.08%</good> increased ballistic and non-beam energy weapon damage for every su/s of the ship's current speed.
flavour|tania_dysis_drive	0	The Black Hawk's Dysis Drive throws the ship forward hardest while its flux grid runs cold. Engineers lent by a Navarchy commission teach the crew to tune this ship's engines the same way, so it surges ahead at low flux and drags once the grid fills.
type|tania_dysis_drive|FRIGATE|0	0	Top speed changes with flux, from <good>+50</good> su/s at no flux to <bad>-50</bad> su/s at full flux, with no change at half flux. Below half flux, also up to <good>50%</good> increased acceleration and turn acceleration.
type|tania_dysis_drive|DESTROYER|0	0	Top speed changes with flux, from <good>+40</good> su/s at no flux to <bad>-40</bad> su/s at full flux, with no change at half flux. Below half flux, also up to <good>40%</good> increased acceleration and turn acceleration.
type|tania_dysis_drive|CRUISER|0	0	Top speed changes with flux, from <good>+30</good> su/s at no flux to <bad>-30</bad> su/s at full flux, with no change at half flux. Below half flux, also up to <good>30%</good> increased acceleration and turn acceleration.
type|tania_dysis_drive|CAPITAL_SHIP|0	0	Top speed changes with flux, from <good>+20</good> su/s at no flux to <bad>-20</bad> su/s at full flux, with no change at half flux. Below half flux, also up to <good>20%</good> increased acceleration and turn acceleration.
flavour|tania_fafnir_breeches	0	Navarchy dockyards at Farige run a flux line beside the ammunition feed in every mount, so a captain can field whatever the last salvage turned up. Mount plans traded by Navarchy quartermasters let the crew rebuild this ship's ballistic mounts the same way, though the shared feed draws harder on the grid each time they fire shells.
type|tania_fafnir_breeches|null|0	0	Ballistic weapon mounts become hybrid mounts.
type|tania_fafnir_breeches|null|1	1	<good>25%</good> increased ballistic weapon flux cost.
type|tania_fafnir_breeches|FRIGATE|0	0	Ballistic weapon mounts become hybrid mounts.
type|tania_fafnir_breeches|FRIGATE|1	1	<good>25%</good> increased ballistic weapon flux cost.
type|tania_fafnir_breeches|DESTROYER|0	0	Ballistic weapon mounts become hybrid mounts.
type|tania_fafnir_breeches|DESTROYER|1	1	<good>25%</good> increased ballistic weapon flux cost.
type|tania_fafnir_breeches|CRUISER|0	0	Ballistic weapon mounts become hybrid mounts.
type|tania_fafnir_breeches|CRUISER|1	1	<good>25%</good> increased ballistic weapon flux cost.
type|tania_fafnir_breeches|CAPITAL_SHIP|0	0	Ballistic weapon mounts become hybrid mounts.
type|tania_fafnir_breeches|CAPITAL_SHIP|1	1	<good>25%</good> increased ballistic weapon flux cost.
flavour|tania_rise_from_the_ashes	0	Carina rose from the ashes of the Battle of Vela, and the Navarchy drills its Sandgrouse crews for the moment their ship should break. Freed Calypso prisoners who sign on aboard teach the crew those drills: rerouting what is left of the hull and throwing every spare plate over the breach, once, before it gives way.
type|tania_rise_from_the_ashes|null|0	0	Once per battle, the hit that would destroy this ship instead leaves it with <good>25%</good> of its maximum hull points.
type|tania_rise_from_the_ashes|null|1	0	Surviving that hit restores <good>50%</good> of maximum armor to every armor cell.
type|tania_rise_from_the_ashes|null|2	0	<good>50%</good> less damage taken for 6 seconds after surviving that hit.
type-detail|tania_rise_from_the_ashes|null|0	0	Can't be allocated on phase ships.
