flavour|wing_scramble	0	Every League member world sends its own carrier detachment to a joint fleet, and the League's flight doctrine makes them fly as one: a bomber from one world takes orders from a flight lead from another. Serving under a League commission, the crew learns to rewire this carrier's wing datalinks the same way, so every flight it launches carries a pilot from each of its bays.
type|wing_scramble|null|0	0	When this ship deploys, its wings that share a role lend each other strikecraft. Each wing keeps at least 1 of its own strikecraft and fills the rest of its normal wing size with up to <good>1</good> of every other strikecraft type in its group. All its wings use the engagement range of its longest-ranged wing. Strikecraft in each group fly at the group's average top speed.
type|wing_scramble|FRIGATE|0	0	When this ship deploys, its wings that share a role lend each other strikecraft. Each wing keeps at least 1 of its own strikecraft and fills the rest of its normal wing size with up to <good>1</good> of every other strikecraft type in its group. All its wings use the engagement range of its longest-ranged wing. Strikecraft in each group fly at the group's average top speed.
